{[Vague form 1]}\label{conjecturevagueformun}
Let $\mathbb{K}$ be an ATR field of degree $n \geq 3$ which we view as a subset of $\mathbb{C}$ via one of its two complex embeddings. Fix an integral ideal $\mathfrak{f} \neq \mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{K}}$. Fix an integral ideal $\mathfrak{b}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{K}}$ representing a class in $\mathrm{Cl}^{+}(\mathfrak{f})$ and an auxiliary integral ideal $\mathfrak{a}$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{K}}$ of norm $N$ such that $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{K}}/\mathfrak{a}$ is cyclic. Then there is an explicit integer $m$ and explicit parameters $z_j$, $\tau_{1, j}, \dots, \tau_{n-1,j}$ in $\mathbb{K}$, all depending on $\mathfrak{f}, \mathfrak{b}, \mathfrak{a}$ such that the evaluation
\begin{equation}\label{uvagueformun}
u = \left(\prod_{j = 1}^{m} \frac{G_{n-2}(z_j, \tau_{1, j}, \dots, \tau_{n-1,j})^N}{G_{n-2}(Nz_j, N\tau_{1, j}, \dots, N\tau_{n-1,j})}\right)^{\mathcal{D}(N, n)}
\end{equation}
is an algebraic unit in the narrow ray class field $\mathbb{K}^{+}(\mathfrak{f})$ (where the integer $\mathcal{D}(N, n)$ is defined by $\mathcal{D}(N, n) = \prod_{p \mid N} p^{\lfloor \frac{n}{p-1} \rfloor} $). In addition, the algebraic unit $u$ satisfies a Kronecker limit formula of the form:
\begin{equation}\label{klfvagueformun}
N \cdot \zeta'_{\mathfrak{f}}(\mathfrak{b}, 0) - \zeta'_{\mathfrak{f}}(\mathfrak{a}\mathfrak{b}, 0) = \frac{1}{\mathcal{D}(N, n)} \log|u|^2.
\end{equation}

