u$ be elements of $\mathbb{K}$ such that $\mathfrak{f}\mathfrak{b}^{-1} = \mathbb{Z} \mu  + \mathbb{Z} 
u$ and $\mathfrak{f}(\mathfrak{a}\mathfrak{b})^{-1} = \mathbb{Z} \mu +\mathbb{Z} 
u/N$ with $\mu/
u = 	au \in \mathbb{K} \cap \mathbb{H}$. Assume further that $
u/q \equiv 1 \mathrm{~mod~} \mathfrak{f}\mathfrak{b}^{-1}$. Then the complex number
$$u_{\mathfrak{b}} =  rac{	heta\left( rac{1}{q}, 	auight)^N}{	heta\left( rac{N}{q}, N	auight)}$$
is a $q$-unit in the ray class field of $\mathbb{K}$ at $\mathfrak{f}$. The Shimura reciprocity law is explicitly given by $\sigma_{\mathfrak{b}'}(u_{\mathfrak{b}}) = u_{\mathfrak{b}\mathfrak{b}'}$ where $\mathfrak{b}' \mapsto \sigma_{\mathfrak{b}'}$ is Artin's map. In addition, $u_{\mathfrak{b}}$ satisfies a version of Kronecker's second limit formula:
